<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pandulf IV of Capua</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 1050</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Wolf of the Abruzzi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pandulf IV was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> prince of Capua who ruled at intervals between 1016 and 1050. Called the Wolf of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abruzzo">Abruzzi</a>, he plundered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monte-cassino">Monte Cassino</a> and fought the princes of Salerno and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a>, hiring Norman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a> who later carved out lordships of their own. The emperor Conrad II deposed him in 1038, but he regained Capua in 1047.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pandulf-iv-of-capua.jpg" alt="Pandulf IV of Capua" width="320" height="406" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kaiser_Heinrich_II._l%C3%A4%C3%9Ft_F%C3%BCrst_Pandulf_IV._von_Capua_gefangensetzen.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
